{"book":23,"chapter":13,"context":{"chapter":13,"title":"The Burden of Babylon","summary":"The first of Isaiah's oracles against the nations targets Babylon: God musters an army for the Day of the Lord, the heavens go dark, and the Medes overthrow Babylon so completely that only wild creatures will live there.","background":"'Burden' (v. 1) translates massa, a weighty prophetic message, usually of judgment. In Isaiah's day Babylon was a restless city under Assyrian rule; later it became the empire that destroyed Jerusalem. The Medes, from what is now Iran, joined the Persians under Cyrus, who took Babylon in 539 BC.","customs":[{"term":"Satyrs","verses":"13:21","note":"The Hebrew means 'hairy ones': wild goats, or goat-like demons believed to haunt ruins. Either way, a picture of utter desolation."}],"watchFor":["'The day of the Lord' (vv. 6, 9) with sun, moon and stars darkened (v. 10), language Jesus echoes in Matthew 24:29.","Babylon will end like Sodom and Gomorrah (v. 19)."],"connections":["Matthew 24:29","Jeremiah 50:39-40","Daniel 5:30-31","Revelation 18:2"]},"verses":{"1":{"w":[["מַשָּׂא","masa'","H4853","HNcmsc","[the] oracle of"],["בָּבֶל","bavel","H894","HNpl","Babylon"],["אֲשֶׁר","'asher","H834","HTr","which"],["חָזָה","chazah","H2372","HVqp3ms","he saw"],["יְשַׁעְיָהוּ","yesha'yahu","H3470","HNpm","Isaiah"],["בֶּן","ben-","H1121","HNcmsc","[the] son of"],["אָמוֹץ","'amotz","H531","HNpm","Amoz"]],"x":[[23047001,23047015,6],[24050001,24051064,6],[23001001,23001001,5],[27005006,27005006,4],[27005028,27005028,4],[66017001,66017018,4],[23013019,23013019,3],[23014004,23014023,3],[23014028,23014028,3],[23015001,23015001,3]],"xn":12},"2":{"w":[["עַל","'al","H5921","HR","on"],["הַר","har-","H2022","HNcmsa","a mountain"],["נִשְׁפֶּה","nishpeh","H8192","HVNrmsa","swept bare"],["שְׂאוּ","se'u-","H5375","HVqv2mp","lift up"],["נֵס","nes","H5251","HNcmsa","a standard"],["הָרִימוּ","harimu","H7311","HVhv2mp","lift up"],["קוֹל","kol","H6963","HNcmsa","a voice"],["לָהֶם"